2026-05-14  Ivan S. Titov  <iohann.s.titov@gmail.com>

	2.0.0_rc2 — "First CI Run + Packaging Polish"

	Three CI cycles on gentoo/stage3:latest after rc1 surfaced 5
	shellcheck --severity=error violations (rc1 dev host didn't have
	shellcheck installed locally; make distcheck passed but the CI
	`shellcheck --severity=error src/portconf` step failed before any
	test tier ran).  Fixes for all five are below, plus the routine
	work of preparing the audited tree for release: Gentoo ebuilds,
	editor/shellcheck config baselines, a CI-locked dist sanity-check,
	GitHub issue templates and contribution guide, AI-assistance
	disclosure.  281 bats tests pass (178 unit + 70 integration +
	32 smoke + 1 root-conditional) against a shellcheck-clean source.

	Source-side fixes:
	* src/portconf.in (sort_uses, sort_keywords): SC2066 — the
	  `for option in "$(...)"` loop pattern (double-quoted command
	  substitution) iterates exactly once.  Replaced with a direct
	  `atom_opts+="$(...)"` append; same semantics, less code.
	* src/portconf.in (mask_trash slot_output / non_slot_output):
	  SC2104 — `continue 2` inside an inner function works in bash
	  (the directive propagates up through the function call to the
	  enclosing loop) but is non-portable.  Refactored: the helpers
	  set `_trash_hit=1`; the inner unmask loop adds
	      (( _trash_hit )) && break
	  at the end of its body.  Same control-flow effect — break inner
	  → outer continues naturally — without the function-level loop
	  magic.  Per-outer-iteration `_trash_hit=0` reset added.
	* src/portconf.in (dispatcher tail): SC2199 — `[[ -z "${@}" ]]`
	  works only because `${@}` implicitly concatenates inside [[ ]].
	  Replaced with `[[ $# -eq 0 ]]`.
	* src/portconf.in: SC2199-fix comment rephrasing — shellcheck
	  parsed `# shellcheck SC2199: ...` as a directive (the canonical
	  form is `disable=SCxxxx`) and bailed with SC1072/SC1073 on the
	  second CI run.  Comment now starts with prose; the SC2199
	  reference is preserved in the body.

	Cosmetic shellcheck pass:
	* src/portconf.in: 18 warning-level findings down to 3.  Dead
	  variables removed (newest in backup / world_backup;
	  installed_vers / installed_min_ver / installed_max_ver /
	  installed_live_ver in check_uses).  ${*} for the opts assembly
	  (was implicit ${@}-as-string).  Quoted `$(_cols)` in the three
	  fold-pipeline sites.  `# shellcheck disable=` and
	  `# shellcheck source=/dev/null` directives at the four runtime-
	  resolved source-call sites and the variadic _mktemp forwarder
	  and the intentional column-placeholder `read` in mask_trash.
	  No behaviour change — diff is comments + idiomatic spellings +
	  7 lines of dead code removed.
	* The remaining 3 warnings are SC2010 (`ls | grep`) patterns in
	  repo_fix / f_to_d / d_to_f.  Functional rewrites; explicitly
	  deferred to 2.1.0.

	Tests:
	* tests/unit/diff_ask.bats: root-conditional Yes-branch coverage.
	  The existing "interactive Yes as non-root — exits 1" test
	  passes only as a non-root UID; CI on gentoo/stage3:latest runs
	  as root and would hit the mv+chmod branch instead.  Gated with
	  `(( UID == 0 )) && skip`, plus a complementary root-branch
	  test gated with `(( UID != 0 )) && skip`.  Together they cover
	  both branches in their respective environments.

	Packaging:
	* packaging/portconf.ebuild.in: EAPI=8 release ebuild for the
	  ::stuff overlay.  RDEPEND covers bash 4.4+, eix, portage-utils,
	  tre, portage; bash-completion is optional.  src_test runs the
	  unit suite, probes the eix cache, and conditionally runs the
	  integration suite when the cache is populated.  pkg_postinst
	  reminds about eix-update.
	* packaging/portconf-9999.ebuild: live ebuild inheriting git-r3,
	  no KEYWORDS, with autoconf/automake added to BDEPEND and
	  eautoreconf in src_prepare.
	* packaging/metadata.xml: maintainer, longdesc, USE flag docs,
	  GitHub remote-id.
	* packaging/Makefile.am: `make ebuild OVERLAY_DIR=...` recipe
	  drops a versioned ebuild + metadata.xml into the given overlay
	  and runs `ebuild ... manifest` to fetch the dist tarball and
	  write Manifest.  Top-level Makefile.am delegates.

	Build:
	* .editorconfig: whitespace rules for shells, bats, ebuilds,
	  autoconf, YAML, ChangeLog.  Shipped in EXTRA_DIST.
	* .shellcheckrc: encodes the SC2010 deferrals (3 sites in
	  repo_fix / f_to_d / d_to_f) so local shellcheck matches CI
	  behaviour.
	* Makefile.am: new installcheck-local target — verifies installed
	  $(bindir)/portconf reports the expected version and that
	  --help works.  Honors DESTDIR for staging installs.
	* configure.ac: bump to 2.0.0_rc2.

	CI:
	* .github/workflows/ci.yml: dist sanity-check switched from
	  `make dist` to `make distcheck`.  `make dist` only produces the
	  tarball; `make distcheck` extracts it into an isolated subdir
	  and runs configure + make + make check + make install + make
	  uninstall against it — catches missing EXTRA_DIST entries,
	  srcdir-vs-builddir bugs, and install-target breakage that plain
	  `make dist` would not surface.

	Docs:
	* README.md: CI status badge, markdown links for ChangeLog +
	  INSTALL, ::stuff overlay add-overlay URL.
	* AUTHORS, README.md, ChangeLog: AI usage disclosure block —
	  Claude (Anthropic) used as a coding assistant; every change
	  reviewed by hand and validated against bats unit + integration
	  + smoke + shellcheck + make distcheck before landing.
	* CONTRIBUTING.md: contribution guide covering bug reports,
	  feature proposals, PR workflow (with the new-flag checklist),
	  commit messages, code style, signing, license.
	* .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/{bug_report,feature_request,config}.yml:
	  GitHub issue forms — version + environment + command output +
	  expected/actual + relevant /etc/portage file content (with
	  flag-to-file pairing table); minimal feature template.
	* ChangeLog: corrected stale commit-hash references and the
	  broken rebrand from-to in the rc1 and pre5 entries; added the
	  missing smoke-helper entries (help.bats, profile.bats) to pre5;
	  updated test-count, bug-count, and `|| true` figures to match
	  current state.

	Note: the rc1 tag and the rc1 ChangeLog entry below are preserved
	verbatim — rc1 was a real (failed-CI) state.  rc2 is the same
	source tree plus the post-rc1 fixes, the cosmetic shellcheck
